{"type":"new","contents":"/-\nInfoGeometry/Canonical/CoordinateFree.lean\n\nCoordinate-free invariant core:\nThe modular construction is formulated without chart-dependent primitives as\nfoundational data. Its primitive inputs are:\n  - abstract group actions,\n  - filter-based cusp limits,\n  - stabilizer extraction at orbifold points,\n  - curve/connection data on abstract carriers.\n\nThis file records the chart-free theorem surface at the canonical layer without\nintroducing coordinate grids as primitive objects.\n-/\n\nimport Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Action.Basic\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical\n\n/-- A predicate on an abstract carrier is coordinate-free for a symmetry action when it is\nunchanged by every symmetry. -/\ndef CoordinateFreeInvariant (G : Type*) {X : Type*} [Monoid G] [MulAction G X]\n    (P : X → Prop) : Prop :=\n  ∀ (g : G) (x : X), P (g • x) ↔ P x\n\n/-- Coordinate-free invariance is stable under composition of coordinate changes. -/\ntheorem CoordinateFreeInvariant.comp {X G : Type*} [Monoid G] [MulAction G X] {P : X → Prop}\n    (hP : CoordinateFreeInvariant G P) (g h : G) (x : X) :\n    P ((g * h) • x) ↔ P x := by\n  rw [mul_smul]\n  exact (hP g (h • x)).trans (hP h x)\n\n/-- The chart-free statement for canonical modular invariance: invariant predicates remain\ninvariant after composing abstract coordinate changes. -/\ndef CoordinateFreeContract : Prop :=\n  ∀ {X G : Type*} [Monoid G] [MulAction G X] (P : X → Prop),\n    CoordinateFreeInvariant G P → ∀ (g h : G) (x : X), P ((g * h) • x) ↔ P x\n\n/-- Canonical modular invariance is chart-free at the theorem level. -/\ntheorem coordinateFreeContract : CoordinateFreeContract := by\n  intro X G _ _ P hP g h x\n  exact hP.comp g h x\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical\n","mtime":1778317504434}